WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
The word synagogue comes from a
Greek word meaning to bring together.

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.940
Walk inside and look for a
statue, or a picture of God.

3
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.340
You won't find one.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.160
Instead there are Hebrew words, patterns,

5
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.670
plants, and symbols such
as the twelve tribes.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.660
And wherever it stands, everyone
inside prays facing the same way.

7
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.720
So what does fill a synagogue,
and why does it face Jerusalem?

8
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.960
In this mission, you'll build
a labelled plan of a synagogue,

9
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.650
piece by piece.

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.900
Then you'll compare synagogues
from different Jewish movements,

11
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.470
side by side.

12
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.640
Your mission: find out
what fills a synagogue,

13
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.520
and why it faces Jerusalem.
